Patch 35 -- keep the exact MGS2 AABB scan as a bridgeable diagnostic target.

The production compiler inlines d3d8_mgs2_scan_aabb() into DrawPrimitive.  The
native ARM experiment must identify exactly one reviewed function without
changing its algorithm, so keep only this helper out of line.  Companion Box86
patch 05 recognises its exact prologue and remains off unless
MGS2_BOX86_NATIVE_AABB=1 is set.

This patch alone is expected to be neutral/slightly slower and is not for
production.  Its stripped candidate SHA256 is
4ec1b13f30a8fb603d8f9b627739e81197b5170772afda6c73cc0994ea4ed619.

--- a/dlls/d3d8/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d8/device.c
@@ -2233,1 +2233,2 @@
-static BOOL d3d8_mgs2_scan_aabb(const struct d3d8_vertexbuffer *buffer, unsigned int left,
+static __attribute__((noinline)) BOOL d3d8_mgs2_scan_aabb(
+        const struct d3d8_vertexbuffer *buffer, unsigned int left,
